  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 12, P = 26. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[4, 17, 16, 17, 19, 4, 15, 23, 2, 24, 6, 16], [25, 11, 5, 5, 4, 22, 12, 2, 10, 14, 19, 12], [12, 20, 25, 12, 21, 1, 16, 14, 9, 12, 19, 22]], sigma = [8, 11, 9, 4, 3, 10, 7, 6, 0, 2, 5, 1], B = [0, 25, 10, 20, 20, 9, 15, 15, 0, 10, 9, 25].",
